content.text:
I notice I have a syntax issue in `.day-banner` transition — fine.

Also `.step-copy span` has duplicate `display` declarations (block then -webkit-box) — the latter wins, fine.

Now CSS chunk 3: menu, hero, responsive, rotate, desktop. Also fix missing styles for `.game-screen` etc.

Menu:
```
.menu-screen{ z-index:50; background: radial-gradient...; padding: calc(18px + env(safe-area-inset-top)) 20px calc(16px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom)); justify-content:space-between; transition: opacity .4s, transform .4s; }
.menu-screen.out{ opacity:0; transform:translateY(-20px); pointer-events:none; }
```
The menu should be shown initially. The game screen behind is visible but covered.

Hero: flex 1, min-height 0, display grid place-items center; hero-art width min(100%, 300px). On 390x844, the menu has head ~50, copy ~110, actions ~130, hero ~450. Good. On shorter, shrink.

Hero tags positioned.

Menu title h1 30px with em in orange.

Ghost buttons.

Desktop frame: 
```
@media (min-width:560px){
 body{ display:grid; place-items:center; background: radial-gradient(...), #04080b; }
 body::before{ content:''; ... } // ambient
 #app{ width:420px; height:min(880px,96dvh); border-radius:34px; box-shadow:0 40px 100px #000c, 0 0 0 1px #ffffff14, 0 0 0 9px #0a1217; }
}
```
But `#app` height:100dvh; override. Also `position:relative` stays. On mobile <560 no frame.

Add a subtle desktop caption via body::after? Not needed.

Rotate hint:
```
.rotate-hint{ display:none; position:fixed; inset:0; z-index:100; ... }
@media (orientation:landscape) and (max-height:560px){ .rotate-hint{ display:flex } }
```

Responsive small heights:
```
@media (max-height:740px){ ... reduce customer text, phone max, etc. }
```
Also `@media (max-height:680px)` hide `.brand-txt span`, reduce padding, tray 68px, dock etc.

Wide 390 normal.

Need to ensure the dock doesn't overlap the tray. `.mat` bottom:82px to end above tray.

Let me write the rest.

