CSS needed. I'll append CSS later.

The `cracks` element is inside screenLayer. `cracks.style.display='none'` for internal jobs. For the screen job visible.

For the screen job after removing the old screen, we add `.open`? If we add `.open`, the screen layer hides, revealing the interior. But `.open` also is used for reassembly. For the screen job, after removal we can use `.screen-gone` (which hides the screen) and `.interior` opacity 1 (I have `.phone.screen-gone .interior`). Then when installing the new screen, remove `.screen-gone` and show the screen with `.fresh`. Good.

